      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\) to a decimal**:\n   \\[\n   -\\frac{5}{3} \\approx -1.6667\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the floor function**:\n   The floor function, \\(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor\\), gives the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\n3. **Apply the floor function**:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lfloor -1.6667 \\right\\rfloor\n   \\]\n   Since \\(-1.6667\\) is between \\(-2\\) and \\(-1\\), the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\) is \\(-2\\).\n\nPutting this all together, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -2\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2}\n\\]",
